From: eelgaev <3100771+eelgaev@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] nvidia-uvm: check NPU and MM APIs before enabling ATS

UVM_CAN_USE_MMU_NOTIFIERS() excludes PPC64LE kernels >= 5.9 even when
conftest detects the production pnv_npu2_init_context() callback API.
uvm_ats_init() also requires uvm_va_space_mm_enabled_system(), which uses
this macro, so selecting the kernel ATS implementation alone is not
enough: CUDA still reports no pageable-memory access.

The restored NPU API alone is insufficient: enabling VA-space/mm support
also introduces mmput() and __mmdrop() imports. UVM inherits proprietary
taint from nvidia.ko and cannot resolve GPL-only exports of these functions.
Check both export presence and export type using NVIDIA's existing symbol
conftests before enabling the newer-kernel path. This keeps UVM loadable
with ATS disabled on kernels whose MM lifecycle exports are unusable.

Keep the existing notifier and architecture checks and require the
production NPU context API, which selects kernel-provided invalidation.
The pre-5.9 path retains its existing behavior.

Signed-off-by: eelgaev <3100771+eelgaev@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 nvidia-uvm/nvidia-uvm.Kbuild |  4 ++++
 nvidia-uvm/uvm_linux.h      | 13 ++++++++++++-
 2 files changed, 16 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/nvidia-uvm/nvidia-uvm.Kbuild b/nvidia-uvm/nvidia-uvm.Kbuild
--- a/nvidia-uvm/nvidia-uvm.Kbuild
+++ b/nvidia-uvm/nvidia-uvm.Kbuild
@@ -117,3 +117,7 @@ NV_CONFTEST_TYPE_COMPILE_TESTS += mmu_interval_notifier
 
 NV_CONFTEST_SYMBOL_COMPILE_TESTS += is_export_symbol_present_int_active_memcg
 NV_CONFTEST_SYMBOL_COMPILE_TESTS += is_export_symbol_present_migrate_vma_setup
+NV_CONFTEST_SYMBOL_COMPILE_TESTS += is_export_symbol_present_mmput
+NV_CONFTEST_SYMBOL_COMPILE_TESTS += is_export_symbol_gpl_mmput
+NV_CONFTEST_SYMBOL_COMPILE_TESTS += is_export_symbol_present___mmdrop
+NV_CONFTEST_SYMBOL_COMPILE_TESTS += is_export_symbol_gpl___mmdrop

diff --git a/nvidia-uvm/uvm_linux.h b/nvidia-uvm/uvm_linux.h
--- a/nvidia-uvm/uvm_linux.h
+++ b/nvidia-uvm/uvm_linux.h
@@ -128,9 +128,20 @@ static inline const struct cpumask *uvm_cpumask_of_node(int node)
 // The callback was added in commit 0f0a327fa12cd55de5e7f8c05a70ac3d047f405e,
 // v3.19 (2014-11-13) and renamed in commit 1af5a8109904.
+//
+// Newer kernels need both the production NPU API and usable MM lifecycle
+// exports. UVM inherits proprietary taint from nvidia.ko, so GPL-only
+// mmput()/__mmdrop() exports cannot support the VA-space/mm association
+// required by uvm_ats_init().
     #if (defined(NV_MMU_NOTIFIER_OPS_HAS_INVALIDATE_RANGE) || \
          defined(NV_MMU_NOTIFIER_OPS_HAS_ARCH_INVALIDATE_SECONDARY_TLBS)) && \
-        defined(NVCPU_PPC64LE) && LINUX_VERSION_CODE < KERNEL_VERSION(5, 9, 0)
+        defined(NVCPU_PPC64LE) && \
+        (LINUX_VERSION_CODE < KERNEL_VERSION(5, 9, 0) || \
+         (defined(NV_PNV_NPU2_INIT_CONTEXT_CALLBACK_RETURNS_VOID) && \
+          NV_IS_EXPORT_SYMBOL_PRESENT_mmput && \
+          !NV_IS_EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL_mmput && \
+          NV_IS_EXPORT_SYMBOL_PRESENT___mmdrop && \
+          !NV_IS_EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL___mmdrop))
         #define UVM_CAN_USE_MMU_NOTIFIERS() 1
     #else
         #define UVM_CAN_USE_MMU_NOTIFIERS() 0
     #endif
